`o 46A r 1(7)(a) this Order applies to and in relation to the action on the date in question` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the order placing the action on the Express Track was made`
    WHEN JUST placed THEN
        IF `the date in question` AT LEAST placed
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on and after the making of the order"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when a Court makes an order for an action to be placed on the Express Track" is a "when" condition, and no such order has been made (fork 46A.5)

