        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on and after the making of the order"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when a Court makes an order for the removal of an action from the Express Track" is a "when" condition, and no such order has been made (fork 46A.5)

