        IF `o 46A r 1(7)(a) this Order applies to and in relation to the action on the date in question` `the date the order placing the action on the Express Track was made` `the date in question` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): this Order applies "on and after the making of the order" placing the action, and the date is before it
        IF `o 46A r 1(7)(b) this Order has ceased to apply to and in relation to the action on the date in question` `the date the order for the removal of the action from the Express Track was made` `the date in question` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): this Order "ceases to apply ... on and after the making of the order" for removal
